/** @mainpage Qore SSH2 Module

    @tableofcontents

    @section ssh2intro Introduction to the ssh2 Module

    The ssh2 module provides Qore the possibility to communicate with sshd servers via the <a href="http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Secure_Shell#Version_2.x">ssh2 protocol</a>; the underlying functionality is provided by <a href="http://www.libssh2.org">libssh2</a>.

    This module is released under a choice of two licenses:
    - <a href="http://www.gnu.org/licenses/old-licenses/lgpl-2.1.html">LGPL 2.1</a>
    - MIT (see COPYING.MIT in the source distribution for more information)
    .
    The module is tagged as such in the module's header (meaning it can be loaded unconditionally regardless of how the %Qore library was initialized).  This version of the module requires Qore 0.8.1+ to compile and run.

    To use the module in a %Qore script, use the \c %%requires directive as follows:
    @code %requires ssh2 @endcode

    This module provides the following classes:
    |!Class|!Description
    |Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base|base class for @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient "SFTPClient" and @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client "SSH2Client"
    |Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client|allows Qore programs to establish an ssh2 connection to a remote server
    |Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient|allows Qore programs to use the sftp protocol
    |Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel|allows Qore programs to send and receive data through an ssh2 channel
    |Qore::SSH2::SSH2Listener|represents a reverse port forwarding listener (created by SSH2Client::forwardListen())

    Also included with the binary ssh2 module:
    - <a href="../../Ssh2Connections/html/index.html">Ssh2Connections user module</a>
    - <a href="../../SftpClientDataProvider/html/index.html">SftpClientDataProvider user module</a>
    - <a href="../../SftpPollerUtil/html/index.html">SftpPollerUtil user module</a>
    - <a href="../../SftpPoller/html/index.html">SftpPoller user module</a>

    When connecting the module will try to:

    - connect to the server with the given port or with port 22 if no port is given
    - login as the given user (user is set in the URL given to @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client::constructor() "SSH2Client::constructor()" or @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::constructor() "SFTPClient::constructor()" or can be modified with @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setUser() "SSH2Base::setUser()") using:
      - SSH agent authentication (enabled by default; can be disabled with @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setUseAgent() "SSH2Base::setUseAgent()")
      - publickey authentication from memory (set with @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setKeysFromData() "SSH2Base::setKeysFromData()")
      - publickey authentication from file (public and private key files can be modified with @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setKeys() "SSH2Base::setKeys()")
      - password authentication (password can be set in the URL given to @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client::constructor() "SSH2Client::constructor()" or @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::constructor() "SFTPClient::constructor()" or can be set afterwards with @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setPassword() "SSH2Base::setPassword()")
      - keyboard-interactive authentication (faked with password)

    See some examples here: @ref examples

    @section thread_safety Thread Safety

    All classes in this module (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client "SSH2Client", @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient "SFTPClient", and @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel "SSH2Channel") are thread-safe. Internal locking ensures that concurrent access from multiple threads is handled correctly.

    However, note the following considerations:
    - A single connection should not be shared across threads for performance-critical operations, as thread contention may occur
    - @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel "SSH2Channel" objects are tied to their parent @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client "SSH2Client" or @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient "SFTPClient" connection and share the same lock
    - For high-throughput scenarios, consider using separate connection objects per thread

    @section best_practices Best Practices

    @subsection timeout_values Timeout Values
    - Default connection timeout: 60 seconds
    - Default operation timeout: 60 seconds (for SFTP operations)
    - For high-latency networks, consider increasing timeouts
    - For interactive applications, consider shorter timeouts with retry logic

    @subsection connection_management Connection Management
    - Use @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::connected() "connected()" to check connection state before operations
    - Handle connection failures gracefully; the module will auto-disconnect on timeout errors
    - For long-running applications, implement reconnection logic

    @subsection error_handling Error Handling
    - All methods that can fail throw exceptions; use try/catch blocks
    - Common exceptions: \c SSH2-ERROR, \c SSH2CLIENT-TIMEOUT, \c SFTPCLIENT-TIMEOUT
    - Check the \c authenticated key in @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client::info() "info()" to verify successful authentication

    @section examples Examples

    Example of a basic sftp connection:

    @code{.py}
# create object
SFTPClient sftp("sftp://user:pass@host.com:22");
# connect to sftp server
sftp.connect();@endcode

    Example of logging in via ssh2 and executing a command and retrieving the output:

    @code{.py}
# set URL
string url = "sftp://user:pass@host.com:22";
# create object
SSH2Client ssh2(url);
# connect to remote sshd daemon
ssh2.connect();
# get a session channel
SSH2Channel chan = sc.openSessionChannel();
# execute a command on the channel
chan.exec("ls -l");
# retrieve the output and print it out
stdout.printf("%s", chan.read());
# close channel
chan.sendEof();
chan.close();
# print out the exit status after the channel is closed
stdout.printf("exit status: %d\n", chan.getExitStatus());@endcode

    @section codetags Function and Method Tags

    @subsection NOOP NOOP

    Code with this flag makes no calculations, but rather returns a constant value. This flag is given to function and method variants that return a default value depending on the type of argument(s).  When variants with this flag are resolved at parse time, a \c "call-with-type-errors" warning is raised (assuming this warning is enabled), unless \c PO_REQUIRE_TYPES or \c PO_STRICT_ARGS is set.  If \c PO_REQUIRE_TYPES or \c PO_STRICT_ARGS is set, then these variants are inaccessible at parse time; resolving to a variant with this flag set at parse time causes an exception to be thrown.

    These variants are included for backwards-compatibility with qore prior to version 0.8.0 for functions that would ignore type errors in arguments.

    This tag is equal to @ref RUNTIME_NOOP, except no runtime effect is caused by resolving a function or method tagged with \c NOOP at runtime; this tag only affects parse time resolution.

    @subsection RUNTIME_NOOP RUNTIME_NOOP

    Code with this flag makes no calculations, but rather returns a constant value.  This flag is given to function and method variants that return a default value depending on the type of argument(s).  When variants with this flag are resolved at parse time, a \c "call-with-type-errors" warning is raised (assuming this warning is enabled), unless \c PO_REQUIRE_TYPES or \c PO_STRICT_ARGS is set.  If \c PO_REQUIRE_TYPES or \c PO_STRICT_ARGS is set, then these variants are inaccessible; resolving to a variant with this flag set at parse time or run time causes an exception to be thrown.

    These variants are included for backwards-compatibility with qore prior to version 0.8.0 for functions that would ignore type errors in arguments.

    This tag is equal to @ref NOOP, except that \c RUNTIME_NOOP is also enforced at runtime.

    @subsection RET_VALUE_ONLY RET_VALUE_ONLY

    This flag indicates that the function or method has no side effects; it only returns a value, for example.

    This tag is identical to @ref CONSTANT except that functions or methods tagged with \c RET_VALUE_ONLY could throw exceptions.

    @subsection CONSTANT CONSTANT

    This flag indicates that the function or method has no side effects and does not throw any exceptions.

    This tag is identical to @ref RET_VALUE_ONLY except that functions or methods tagged with \c CONSTANT do not throw exceptions.

    @subsection DEPRECATED DEPRECATED

    Code with this flag is deprecated and may be removed in a future version of this module; if a variant with this flag is resolved at parse time, a \c "deprecated" warning is raised (assuming this warning is enabled).

    @section ssh2releasenotes Release Notes

    @subsection ssh2v200 ssh2 Module Version 2.0.0
    Major feature release closing all client-side feature gaps in the libssh2 wrapper.

    <b>Authentication Enhancements:</b>
    - added SSH agent authentication support; tried automatically before other methods
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setUseAgent() "SSH2Base::setUseAgent()")
    - added public key authentication from memory without temp files
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setKeysFromData() "SSH2Base::setKeysFromData()")

    <b>Security - Known Hosts Verification:</b>
    - added known hosts file support for host key verification
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setKnownHostsFile() "SSH2Base::setKnownHostsFile()",
      @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setVerifyHostKey() "SSH2Base::setVerifyHostKey()")
    - configurable host key policy: REJECT (default) or TOFU (Trust On First Use)
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setHostKeyPolicy() "SSH2Base::setHostKeyPolicy()")
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::getHostKey() "SSH2Base::getHostKey()" returning MD5/SHA1/SHA256 fingerprints
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::addKnownHost() "SSH2Base::addKnownHost()" for manual host key management
    - added \c SSH2_HOSTKEY_REJECT and \c SSH2_HOSTKEY_TOFU constants

    <b>Session Configuration:</b>
    - added algorithm preference control
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setMethodPreference() "SSH2Base::setMethodPreference()")
    - added supported algorithm query
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::getSupportedAlgorithms() "SSH2Base::getSupportedAlgorithms()")
    - added SSH banner control
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setBanner() "SSH2Base::setBanner()",
      @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::getBanner() "SSH2Base::getBanner()")
    - added configurable keepalive interval
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setKeepalive() "SSH2Base::setKeepalive()")
    - added debug/trace support with \c SSH2_TRACE_* constants
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Base::setTraceLevel() "SSH2Base::setTraceLevel()")

    <b>Channel Operations:</b>
    - added PTY window resize support
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel::requestPtySize() "SSH2Channel::requestPtySize()")
    - added exit signal retrieval
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel::getExitSignal() "SSH2Channel::getExitSignal()")
    - added signal sending to remote processes
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel::sendSignal() "SSH2Channel::sendSignal()")
    - added SSH agent forwarding on channels
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Channel::requestAuthAgent() "SSH2Channel::requestAuthAgent()")
    - added Unix domain socket forwarding
      (@ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client::openDirectStreamLocalChannel() "SSH2Client::openDirectStreamLocalChannel()")

    <b>Reverse Port Forwarding:</b>
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Listener "SSH2Listener" class for reverse port forwarding
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SSH2Client::forwardListen() "SSH2Client::forwardListen()" to create remote listeners
    - equivalent to \c "ssh -R" reverse tunneling

    <b>SFTP Operations:</b>
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::symlink() "SFTPClient::symlink()" - create symbolic links
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::readlink() "SFTPClient::readlink()" - read symlink targets
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::lstat() "SFTPClient::lstat()" - stat without following symlinks
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::chown() "SFTPClient::chown()" - change file ownership
    - added @ref Qore::SSH2::SFTPClient::statvfs() "SFTPClient::statvfs()" - filesystem statistics

    <b>SCP Improvements:</b>
    - updated to use \c libssh2_scp_recv2() and \c libssh2_scp_send64() for proper 64-bit file size support

    <b>Data Provider Updates:</b>
    - added symlink, readlink, chown, lstat, and statvfs data providers

    <b>Connection Module Updates:</b>
    - added \c known_hosts, \c verify_host_key, \c use_agent, and \c keepalive_interval connection options

    <b>Bug Fixes:</b>
    - removed stale TODO in mkdir implementation
    - documented known memory leak in sftp_shutdown timeout (libssh2 limitation)
    - updated copyright years to 2026

